@bestcornishcat Well I'm in a position to do so and know that there are many others too. And there are people who are willing to travel with "strangers". A former co-worker of mine for example was looking for max. 2 crew members for a 4 months sailing trip around the Bay of Biscay and placed an ad, he couldn't find two passengers he deemed fit for his trip so finally he picked the one person he felt comfortable on they went.

I'm an experienced traveller, have been around the world and met all kind of expats and travellers/backpacker, some of them had just met on the road and decided to travel a couple days or weeks together. In Sri Lanka I once spontaneously rented this double unit condo together with someone I'd just met in a bar. You know just because you lack the imagination why people would want to travel or stay abroad with someone they don't know for years doesn't mean that these people - rational or not so rational - exist and that it happens daily. As for your other recomandations concerning who pays what, habits, emergency, early return and so forth that's just common sense, of course you discuss that while planing in advance.



@Mondial

There are lots of travel buddies sites, a simple google search came up with about 15 - 20 sites and I'm in the process of going through them. But I asked for a site specialized for people with disabilities and sometimes there are sites who have real useful boards almost hidden inside and these sites don't always turn up easily on google. Actually I'm open for any medium, print media f.e. would be fine too. Someone recently made me aware of a pretty obscure newsletter in print (they don't even have a website) for people with disabilities, families and caregivers and there is an ad section too where people are looking for all kind of things, romance, shared flats, activities and travel companions. Basically I asked for info because chances are that in this forum section here someone with experience and knowledge might respond. I get it, you three think that searching a travel companion online is unwise or dangerous but I don't. So spare me the warnings please. And I didn't claim to be special and I know I'm not alone. That's actually Dawkin's point in "The God Delusion", that the human species is not special or the center of the universe, that the universe is indifferent to human suffering and that the fact that life has no meaning is the sole reason to live. But our existence as a species or individual if you will can have genuine meaning but you must supply your own fulfillment within the boundaries of life and death. I hold him in high regard because his books taught me a lot, he encouraged me to embrace life and part of life is taking risks.

